Indexer builds field lengths rowwise: a load into a columnar table with field lengths is refused at once, empty or not, and the table keeps its definition.
––– input –––
source /tmp/bi.sh; bi_sql "CREATE TABLE bulk_lens (title text, a int) engine='columnar' index_field_lengths='1'"; bi_load bulk_lens "(id,title,a) VALUES (1,'three',1)" 2>&1; bi_sql "INSERT INTO bulk_lens (id,title,a) VALUES (2,'one two',2); FLUSH RAMCHUNK bulk_lens"; bi_load bulk_lens "(id,title,a) VALUES (3,'three',3)" 2>&1; bi_sql "SELECT id, title_len FROM bulk_lens"
––– output –––
ERROR 1064 (42000) at line 1: bulk_import does not support columnar field lengths (attribute 'title_len')
ERROR 1064 (42000) at line 1: bulk_import does not support columnar field lengths (attribute 'title_len')
2	2
––– comment –––
A loaded chunk is ready at once: COUNT(*) over field lengths is answered by the secondary index right after the load (12000 rows, 4000 each with 0, 1 and 2 words).
––– input –––
source /tmp/bi.sh; bi_sql "CREATE TABLE bulk_si (title text) index_field_lengths='1'"; seq 1 12000 | awk 'BEGIN { print "SET bulk_import=bulk_si;" } { printf "%s(%d,\047%s\047)", ($1%1000==1 ? "INSERT INTO bulk_si (id,title) VALUES " : ","), $1, ($1%3==0 ? "" : ($1%3==1 ? "one" : "one two")) } $1%1000==0 { print ";" } END { print "COMMIT; SET bulk_import=0;" }' | mysql -h0 -P9306; bi_sql "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bulk_si WHERE title_len=1; SHOW META LIKE 'index'" | xargs
––– output –––
4000 index title_len:Precalc (100%)
